print of "=== HALTING: SETTLED CONSTANT TEST (#861) ==="
print of "--- HS1: a constant at moderate H certifies converged ---"
# Pre-#861 this pinned the dead zone: H(42) ~ 0.16 sat above h_low, so the
# entropy `converged` could never fire on a constant at 42 and the strongest
# claim was "equilibrium". The value route certifies a settled value at ANY
# magnitude — that was the point of the fix.

x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42
x is 42

# Read both predicates against x in one expression — a separate `c is converged`
# would repoint the last-observer alias to c before `equilibrium` is read.
hs1 is [converged, equilibrium]

print of hs1[0]
print of hs1[1]

print of ""
print of "--- HS2: the entropy MEASUREMENT is unchanged ---"

print of where is x
print of why is x
print of report of x

print of ""
print of "=== SETTLED CONSTANT COMPLETE ==="
